+# N27 named Hydra continuation — CPU implementation contract
+
+This source prepares one new administrative continuation. It does not authorize a GPU launch, adopt a budget, or turn original N27 INVALID into a scientific result. The original source is 095cfeecd6af55477d2529441c307ab712e8a8da. Its 345-file record is tracked alongside this document. Only configs/config.yaml and the four explicitly listed runner/worker routing functions differ; whole-file reversal is in reverse-source-v1.json. All policy, native/reference, profiles, provider, runtime and worker run_worker/verify_receipt bytes remain original. There is no new numerical preflight.
+
+## Paths and immutability
+
+All new control artifacts live at N27/hydra-continuation-v1 (RUN_DIR), independently of the original attempt artifact volume. New attempt outputs remain under frozen plan.artifact_root/attempts. The supervisor creates RUN_DIR/execution before its lock. It refuses any previous status/result/controller record or reservation; it never resumes. CLI scripts automatically put scripts/ on sys.path and explicitly add the owning worktree root. Root must run from the adopted owning worktree, not the isolated implementation checkout.
+
+The three changed existing files are configs/config.yaml; scripts/qd_ed_final_runner.py (metered_support, check_budget, check_retry); scripts/qd_ed_n23_worker.py (validate_context only). New plans keep n27_cohort with the exact old WORKER_CONTRACT so unchanged same-process run_worker and verify_receipt retain N27 profile-bound checks, including zero-guided episodes. The additional n27_hydra_continuation marker takes priority only in the administrative routing. Mixed or incomplete plans fail the new exact contract. Old N27 plans retain the old branch.
+
+## Root-made history seal (not generated or read by CPU executor)
+
+Write history-seal-v1.json with schema n27-hydra-history-seal-v1. Field names below are exact. Refs are absolute resolved path + SHA256; full source records are {commit,files:[{path,sha256}],sha256}, sorted by path with canonical JSON file-list digest. The runtime is its unchanged old ref, not a new manifest. See qd_ed_n27_cont_history.verify for executable pure constraints.
+
+- original_disposition: INVALID_OR_INTERRUPTED; original_source: exact old345 record.
+- original_plan: old frozen ref (SHA8632a2f...); original_plan_content: its exact JSON object; original_plan_content_sha256: worker.canonical_sha(object), distinct from the file-byte SHA.
+- root_terminal_review: SHA01dc887d...; startup_classification: SHA276985ca...; original_result: unchanged INVALID result ref.
+- original_source_review, original_authority, historical_backend_proof, budget_authority: original control refs. Budget authority is the existing N26 522/100 finite authority, not an old N27 limit record.
+- runtime: {path: oldplan.runtime_manifest_path,sha256: oldplan.runtime_manifest_sha256}.
+- old_events: all original N27 events, exact ordered 4 × reserved/dispatched/valid, including the original invalid's literal fields; no full private ledger. all_old_attempts: four {attempt_id,episode_key,profile,terminal} wrappers with terminal exactly equal to each last event. Do not change its task_failure label or impute missing usage.
+- accepted_prefix: exact3 entries {logical_index:0..2,cell,native,auxiliary}. cell has episode_key,task_id,profile,attempt_id,success and audit/worker_context/worker_receipt/attempt_result refs, copied from accepted old metadata. All success=false. native/auxiliary are original profile-bound counts. Old commit remains attached to imported cells in the new report.
+- old_resource_events: exact original N27 tensor resource reserved/dispatched/completed subset. Preserve kind/resource_id/cost and all other original fields. old_gpu_seconds equals all4 terminal GPU-process seconds plus proof terminal seconds, without rounding (root-known1401.9772811948787).
+- historical_unknowns: [original_invalid_required_cost_telemetry,original_invalid_provider_usage,original_invalid_native_outcome]. These are still Unknown, never accepted task evidence.
+- cleanup_complete and no_active_owned_worker: true only after root independently checks all known processes/groups and private idle locks.
+
+Root verifies the original same-process receipts/native reports/proof and original closure, then writes root-seal-review-v1.json with the exact object required by contract.history: schema n27-hydra-root-seal-review-v1, accepted=true, seal/protocol/root_terminal_review/startup_classification refs, original_disposition, old_source, historical_backend_proof, native_receipts_attested_not_replayed=true, cleanup_complete=true, gpu_authorized=false. This is an explicit root attestation trust boundary. The new controller follows nine bounded control JSONs (each ≤16MiB) and does not follow their nested tensor/Stage/attempt refs. It does not replay old controller or numerical checks. Current caller-supplied full ledger is filtered and must equal both sealed historical subsets at every capacity/admission check; unrelated cohort appends are allowed.
+
+## Bridge, finite adoption and release
+
+1. Root reviews/commits source and keeps original source intact through historical sealing. Integrate only the reviewed new commit in the idle owning W. Source record comes from w.source_record(W,c.source_paths(vars(r))); do not use the isolated checkout path as future owning root.
+2. Under private locks verify old history, current GPU7 UUID/EGL/owner idle and runtime/provider/source bytes. Build bridge with c.bridge.build(source,c.history(),W); write immutable source-bridge-v1.json. The bridge ties old proof ref to unchanged numerical bytes; it is not a newly generated GPU proof.
+3. Write final-source-runtime-review-v1.json exactly as c.final_review expects: schema n27-hydra-source-runtime-review-v1, accepted=true, source/runtime/protocol/seal/root_seal_review/source_bridge/historical_backend_proof, no_new_preflight=true,gpu_authorized=false.
+4. Write adoption-v1/authority.json exactly as c.authority expects: schema n27-hydra-authority-v1,cohort_id,source,runtime,protocol,seal,final_review,budget_authority,caps,limits,old_gpu_seconds,recorded_at,authority_interpretation,validation_authorized=false,formal_authorized=false. Adopt only state.n27_hydra_continuation_authority={path,sha256}; preserve budget values and original authority records. Do not modify old event buckets/labels. No new GPU proof slot.
+5. From W run `/home/hynx/miniconda3/envs/vla-pilot/bin/python scripts/qd_ed_n27_cont_prepare.py --freeze --output <RUN_DIR>/plan.frozen.v1.gpu7.json`. This requires source/review/adoption and complete remaining full-row capacity before an immutable write. It preserves the old profiles/runtime/seed inputs and all13 original suffix rows except cohort/key and the sole first recovery marker. Root separately verifies actual13 commands/provider/resources before release. No automatic rollback/re-freeze of a failed frozen plan.
+6. Write execution-release-v1.json exactly as supervise.release_check expects: schema n27-hydra-execution-release-v1,plan,source_commit,cohort_id,authority,seal,episode_keys (all13 fixed order),limits,one_launch=true,physical_gpu=7,validation_authorized=false,formal_authorized=false.
+7. Launch once: `/home/hynx/miniconda3/envs/vla-pilot/bin/python scripts/qd_ed_n27_cont_supervise.py --plan <RUN_DIR>/plan.frozen.v1.gpu7.json --release <RUN_DIR>/execution-release-v1.json --status <RUN_DIR>/execution/supervisor-status-v1.json`. Original runner owns reservation, locks, process launch, 1800s timeout+40s cleanup, same-process audit, charging and terminal append. This preparation does not run those commands.
+
+Exact unchanged caps:522 attempts/100 GPUh; baseline62,development220,validation180,formal40,recovery20; unspent protected allocations32h/12h retained. First new row is only the named original ...__1af7d45d9a10 replacement, charged recovery; other12 are baseline3/development9. No extra typed timeout recovery. Before launch and every row require all still-unrun rows ×1840s to fit remaining combined9.25h and cumulative unprotected allowance, plus all remaining slots. old4+new13=17 episode dispatches maximum,16 logical cells. Missing original telemetry stays missing; all measured elapsed costs remain.
+
+## Terminal semantics
+
+New result-v1.json has schema n27-hydra-continuation-result-v1, original_disposition always INVALID_OR_INTERRUPTED, continuation_disposition COMPLETE_THIRTEEN_VALID only after all13 new valid cells, otherwise INVALID_OR_INTERRUPTED. `decision` is the combined logical16 screen. Full promotion requires N27≥2/4,≥every control,strictly>N26, and substantive QD/ED. It grants only separately frozen full Dev consideration. Complete failure is REJECT_SCREEN; any incomplete/invalid/status-journal mismatch is INVALID_OR_INTERRUPTED. No ten-task futility rule. Zero gradients/zero-guided episodes are not individual efficacy vetoes, but all profile-bound audit gates remain required.
+
+Report aggregates all17 possible episode attempts, preserving unknown usage via null/missing lists and partial observed token totals. The proof is retained in the seal/source bridge and charged in combined local admission; all_attempt_costs describes episodes, not resource proofs. An exception after a valid terminal append preserves that valid journal prefix and costs while marking controller mismatch INVALID. Any newly invalid episode stops; no catch-and-retry. Root independently reviews terminal metadata and cleanup after closure; this implementation adds no generic terminal reader or downstream release.
+
+All external delivered templates have executable=false/unresolved refs and are not acceptable real authority/release schemas. No validation/formal/protected input or new algorithm is authorized by these artifacts.
