+# N27 exact infrastructure continuation — prospective root design
+
+This is a root design under the continuing explicitly authorized Arbor task, not an execution release. The original N27 cohort, source095cfee, plan, four attempt records, result and independent terminal review remain immutable. Its disposition stays INVALID_OR_INTERRUPTED. The original candidate has no valid outcome; this fault does not reject its scientific hypothesis.
+
+## Evidence and repair scope
+
+Root terminal review `../root-terminal-review-v1.json`, SHA256 `01dc887dc20d6050a498b15c575b881a3ad8471041c466818cad1ecb4aa8eaac`, accepted three valid task0 controls and one invalid N27 startup. All six known controller/proof/worker process identities are dead. The failed named attempt is `rdt-qd-ed-final-20260921T093925Z__n27_screen_t00_n27_20261001__1af7d45d9a10`. Its339-byte runner log identifies Hydra's unregistered `main.eds_config.diversity_update_mode`; worker receipt main_exit_code1, audit_seconds0, no audit report. Charged wall time7.231457023997791s stays in development. Missing cost telemetry remains unknown. No Stage timeout eligibility is claimed.
+
+The sole proposed scientific configuration repair is to register `diversity_update_mode: legacy_additive` in configs/config.yaml. Exact spelling is inherited from the existing policy/helper default. N27 retains its already frozen feasible_ray_v1 override. Require real Hydra composition of the original and repaired four-arm complete generated commands, unchanged argv, controls identical after deleting only this explicitly legacy default, and N27 inherited settings unchanged except the intended mode. Do not use broad `+` overrides. No policy/helper/native arithmetic/scorer/model/Stage/provider/runtime/action code changes.
